<title>UK: UAL plans 777s for London-California routes.</title>
<headline>UAL plans 777s for London-California routes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Airlines said it will begin using the long range version of the Boeing 777 on its twice daily non-stop flights between London-San Francisco from March 31.</p>
<p>A second Boeing 777 will start to fly the route from April 11, it added in a statement, replacing the smaller Boeing 767s now in use.</p>
<p>On June 6, the daily London-Los Angeles flight will also begin using a 777 instead of the current 767, it added.</p>
<p>The 292 seat 777 provides both additional range and payload capacity, the airline said.</p>
<p>--Reuter Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44-171-542-7706 Fax+ 5017</p>
